## Problem statement

A list of 10,000 rows re-renders every row whenever one row is toggled and the page janks. Fix the re-render problem and cap the DOM size.

## Expected solution

```ts
import { memo, useCallback, useState, type ReactNode } from 'react';

const ROW_HEIGHT = 36;
const OVERSCAN = 5;

export function VirtualList<T>(props: {
  items: readonly T[];
  height: number;
  renderRow: (item: T, index: number) => ReactNode;
}) {
  const { items, height, renderRow } = props;
  const [scrollTop, setScrollTop] = useState(0);
  const start = Math.max(0, Math.floor(scrollTop / ROW_HEIGHT) - OVERSCAN);
  const end = Math.min(items.length, Math.ceil((scrollTop + height) / ROW_HEIGHT) + OVERSCAN);
  return (
    <div style={{ height, overflowY: 'auto' }} onScroll={(e) => setScrollTop(e.currentTarget.scrollTop)}>
      <div style={{ height: items.length * ROW_HEIGHT, position: 'relative' }}>
        {items.slice(start, end).map((item, i) => (
          <div key={start + i} style={{ position: 'absolute', top: (start + i) * ROW_HEIGHT, height: ROW_HEIGHT, left: 0, right: 0 }}>
            {renderRow(item, start + i)}
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  );
}

interface Todo { id: number; title: string; done: boolean }

const Row = memo(function Row(props: { todo: Todo; onToggle: (id: number) => void }) {
  const { todo, onToggle } = props;
  return (
    <label>
      <input type="checkbox" checked={todo.done} onChange={() => onToggle(todo.id)} /> {todo.title}
    </label>
  );
});

export function TodoList({ initial }: { initial: Todo[] }) {
  const [todos, setTodos] = useState(initial);
  const onToggle = useCallback(
    (id: number) => setTodos((prev) => prev.map((t) => (t.id === id ? { ...t, done: !t.done } : t))),
    [],
  );
  return <VirtualList items={todos} height={360} renderRow={(t) => <Row todo={t} onToggle={onToggle} />} />;
}
```

## Explanation

Two separate problems are solved. Re-rendering: `memo` skips rows whose props are shallow-equal. That only works because `onToggle` is stable (functional `setTodos`, empty dependency array) and unchanged todos keep their object identity when mapped. DOM size: the windowing maths derives the first and last visible index from `scrollTop`, adds overscan to avoid blank flashes, and positions rows absolutely inside a spacer whose height equals the full list. Only about 20 nodes exist regardless of list length. Fixed row height keeps the maths trivial; variable heights need measurement.

## Time and space complexity

Render cost drops from O(n) to O(visible rows) per scroll or toggle. Memory is O(n) for data, O(window) for DOM.

## Edge cases

- Row heights that vary: needs measured sizes and a position index.
- Keyboard navigation and screen readers: windowed rows are absent from the DOM, so use ARIA (`aria-rowcount`, `aria-rowindex`) or a proven library.
- Scroll jumps when items are prepended.
- Index keys: switch to stable ids when rows hold state.

